8. Working Principle
When the system is powered ON, ESP32 initializes all connected sensors and modules.
IR sensors continuously monitor for restricted zones.
Hall effect sensor measures wheel rotation speed.
ESP32 calculates vehicle speed from sensor data.
If the speed exceeds the predefined limit:
Buzzer is activated
Motor speed is reduced using PWM
LCD displays zone and speed information.
The system continuously repeats this process.

